// @test: typecheck-pass
// @tier: 0
// @level: L1
// @tags: context, DI, negative-contexts, violation
// @expect: pass
// @description: A function that forbids a context, calling one that requires it. Reported, but as a WARNING — see the note below.
// @spec: 16-context-system.md Section 1.4 - Negative Contexts

// =============================================================================
// The case this file exists for
// =============================================================================
//
// `using [!Database]` is documented as a compile-time guarantee: the
// function, and everything it calls, may not reach that context.
//
// Until 2026-09-03 nothing enforced it. The one place that built the
// checker's model wrote every requirement through `ContextRequirement::new`,
// which hardcodes `is_negative: false`, so `excluded_contexts` was
// permanently empty and the transitive verifier walked a registry in which
// no function forbade anything. The suite did not notice because the section
// named "Testing Negative Context Violations" in
// L2-standard/context/advanced/context_patterns_complete.vr was commented
// out in full — the guarantee had a heading and no test.
//
// WHY `@expect: pass` FOR A VIOLATION. Measured 2026-09-03 on a built
// compiler: the violation IS detected and reported —
//
//   Function 'must_not_touch_the_database' calls 'reads_the_database'
//   which requires context 'Database', but 'Database' is excluded via
//   `using [!Database]`
//
// — but as a tracing warning, not a diagnostic, so the check exits 0.
// `[context] unresolved_policy` defaults to "error", and its "error"
// arm emits `warn!` exactly like its "warn" arm; the knob has no
// effect today. When that is fixed this file becomes
// `@test: typecheck-fail` with the real code, and the change of
// directive is the record that it happened.

context Database {
    fn query(&self, sql: Text) -> Text;
}

// Requires the context.
fn reads_the_database() using [Database] {
    let _ = Database.query("SELECT 1");
}

// Forbids it — and calls the function that requires it.
// E609: transitive negative context violation.
fn must_not_touch_the_database() using [!Database] {
    reads_the_database();
}

fn main() {
    must_not_touch_the_database();
}
